<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.50%" pitch="-2.90%">
      As a father shows compassion to his children, so the Lord shows compassion to those who fear him.<break time="1800ms"/>

      The psalm shifts here from the cosmic to the intimate.<break time="500ms"/>
      From the height of heaven to the nearness of a parent's hand.<break time="1000ms"/>
      God is not only vast.<break time="500ms"/>
      He is close.<break time="500ms"/>
      He is tender.<break time="500ms"/>
      He is the kind of father who bends down.<break time="1800ms"/>

      For he knows our frame.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He remembers that we are dust.<break time="1800ms"/>

      God is not surprised by your weakness.<break time="500ms"/>
      He made you.<break time="500ms"/>
      He knows what you are made of.<break time="500ms"/>
      He knows the limits of your strength, the edges of your patience, the places where your resolve gives way.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And none of it catches Him off guard.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He remembers that we are dust.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not stone.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not iron.<break time="500ms"/>
      Dust.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Fragile, light, easily scattered by the wind.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And yet He does not look at dust with contempt.<break time="500ms"/>
      He looks at it with compassion.<break time="500ms"/>
      The way a good father looks at a small child who has tried hard and fallen short.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Not with anger.<break time="500ms"/>
      Not with disappointment.<break time="500ms"/>
      But with a love that already knew the fall was coming and prepared the arms to catch.<break time="1800ms"/>

      You do not have to be stronger than you are tonight.<break time="500ms"/>
      You do not have to pretend you are not tired.<break time="500ms"/>
      God knows your frame.<break time="1000ms"/>
      He holds you gently because He knows what you are made of.<break time="1800ms"/>

      You are held.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You are crowned with kindness.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
